==English==
[[File:Tagliacarte.jpg|thumb|right|A letter-opener|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|letter-opener}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-letter opener.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several devices for opening [[letter]]s, either by breaking [[sealing wax|wax seals]] or (as is usually the case today) by cutting open their [[envelope]]s.
## A device shaped like a fixed-blade knife, usually with a [[blunt]] edge; the blunt edge does not [[slice#Verb|slice]] the envelope so much as precisely [[tear#Verb|tear]] it.
##: {{cot|en|paperknife<qq:sometimes [[Appendix:Glossary#broadly|broadly]] synonymous>}}
## The same sort of device but with a sharpened edge, designed to appeal to customers who enjoy a sharpened one (regardless of whether or not it truly [[outperform]]s the [[nonsharp]] counterpart).
## A device incorporating a small [[razor]]-style blade in the [[crotch]] of a U-shaped plastic handle; it [[slice#Verb|slices]] the envelope while being, like a [[safety razor]], unlikely to cut the user accidentally.

